        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Drama is the literary mode in which characters speak and act before an audience (real or imagined). It exists at the intersection of literature and performance — the text is a script for enactment, not a work designed for private reading."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DRAMA.md#003",
      "path": [
        "03-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:03-drama, git-history:literature:03-drama]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
