        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The **Poetics** (c. 335 BCE) is the foundational formal analysis of drama. It is not a prescriptive rulebook — Aristotle is analyzing existing practice (primarily Sophocles' Oedipus Rex). But it was read as prescriptive by Renaissance theorists, producing the \"neoclassical rules.\""
    },
    {
