        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Hamartia** — mistranslated for centuries as \"tragic flaw\" (moral failing). The Greek word means \"error\" or \"missing the mark\" (from archery). It is a mistake — of judgment, knowledge, or action — not a character defect. Oedipus's error is not pride; it is his ignorance of his own origins combined with actions that (necessarily, by the logic of fate) bring about what he feared."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DRAMA.md#017",
      "path": [
        "03-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:03-drama, git-history:literature:03-drama]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "concepts": "[drama]",
        "current_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:drama",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[drama]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nHAMARTIA — CORRECT UNDERSTANDING\n----------------------------------\nNot: moral flaw that deserves punishment\nYes: an error in action or judgment, often from ignorance"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DRAMA.md#018",
      "path": [
        "03-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:03-drama, git-history:literature:03-drama]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "concepts": "[drama]",
        "current_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:drama",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[drama]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Why this matters:\n  The tragic hero is not being punished for vice.\n  Tragedy requires a good person falling through error.\n  A wicked person getting just deserts is not tragedy —\n  it is just punishment narrative."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DRAMA.md#019",
      "path": [
        "03-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:03-drama, git-history:literature:03-drama]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "concepts": "[drama]",
        "current_path": "literature/03-DRAMA.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:drama",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[drama]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Drama",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Aristotle's requirement: the hero must be \"intermediate\"\n  — not completely good (fall would be unjust and shocking)\n  — not completely evil (fall would be satisfying, not pitiful)\n  → Someone good, who makes an error, whose fall is undeserved\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DRAMA.md#020",
      "path": [
        "03-DRAMA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:03-drama, git-history:literature:03-drama]",
